From 6b5dcee601b0d6d0fde52ebf1f251003ed06f9f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logdog2325 <loganjayfisher@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 02:11:36 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] DolphinQt: launcher UX - file picker for the ISO and
 launcher-first startup

Two pieces of user feedback on the XD Netplay launcher:

- The XD checklist row now opens a FILE picker (*.iso *.ciso *.rvz *.gcm
  *.gcz *.wia) instead of a folder picker: users know where their ISO
  is, not what a "game folder" means. The picked file's parent directory
  is registered as a game list path, which is what the game list scanner
  wants. Folder auto-discovery of EMERALD.gba is unchanged and is now
  the optional shortcut rather than the primary flow.

- Launcher-first startup: the XD Netplay Launcher opens automatically in
  front of the main window once the event loop is running (a zero-delay
  QTimer::singleShot at the end of the MainWindow constructor), so a new
  player lands directly in the configure/host/join flow with Dolphin
  behind it. It is suppressed when a game or file argument was passed on
  the command line (pending boot), in batch mode, or if a netplay
  session is already active, and can be turned off permanently with the
  new "Show this launcher at startup" checkbox in the dialog (QSettings
  xdnetplay/showlauncheronstartup, default true).
